{"name":"Glazed Carrot","hex":"#e9692c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"glazed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of eyes: glistening but not focusing on anything in particular; showing no liveliness.","Having a glaze (a coating)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of glaze"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glazed"},{"term":"carrot","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vegetable with a nutritious, juicy, sweet root that is often orange in colour, Daucus carota, family Apiaceae, especially the subspecies sativus.","A shade of orange similar to the flesh of most carrots (also called carrot orange)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat (an animal pelt) with a solution of mercuric nitrate as part of felt manufacture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carrot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carrot","blocks":[{"text":"The carrot is a root vegetable in the umbellifer family Apiaceae. Carrots are typically orange in colour due to their beta-carotene content, which makes them a rich source of vitamin A. Heirloom variants may be white, yellow, red, purple, or black. They are biennial plants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Vegetable-Carrot-Bundle-wStalks.jpg/330px-Vegetable-Carrot-Bundle-wStalks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carrot","wikidata":"Q81"},{"title":"Shades of orange","blocks":[{"text":"In optics, orange has a wavelength between approximately 585 and 620 nm and a hue of 30° in HSV color space. In the RGB color space it is a secondary color numerically halfway between gamma-compressed red and yellow, as can be seen in the RGB color wheel. The complementary color of orange is azure. Orange pigments are largely in the ochre or cadmium families, and absorb mostly blue light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Shades_of_Orange.svg/330px-Shades_of_Orange.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_orange","wikidata":"Q19847194"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Carrots_of_many_colors_cropped.png/500px-Carrots_of_many_colors_cropped.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Carrots_of_many_colors_cropped.png/1280px-Carrots_of_many_colors_cropped.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Carrots_of_many_colors_cropped.png/500px-Carrots_of_many_colors_cropped.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Carrots in a range of colors","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarrots_of_many_colors_cropped.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Carrots_are_up_%282634523693%29.jpg/250px-Carrots_are_up_%282634523693%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Carrots_are_up_%282634523693%29.jpg/500px-Carrots_are_up_%282634523693%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Carrots_are_up_%282634523693%29.jpg/250px-Carrots_are_up_%282634523693%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarrots_are_up_(2634523693).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Daucus_carota_flowers%2C_peen_%27Napoli%27_%281%29.jpg/120px-Daucus_carota_flowers%2C_peen_%27Napoli%27_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/common